blish','closed','closed','','order-receipt','','','2026-07-17 16:14:43','2026-07-17 16:14:43','',17,'https://codesblock.com/member-dashboard/order-receipt/',0,'page','',0),(23,1,'2026-07-17 16:14:43','2026-07-17 16:14:43','[pmpro_levels]','Choose Your Plan','','publish','closed','closed','','choose-your-plan','','','2026-07-17 16:14:43','2026-07-17 16:14:43','',0,'https://codesblock.com/choose-your-plan/',0,'page','',0),(24,1,'2026-07-17 16:14:43','2026-07-17 16:14:43','[codesblock_social_login][pmpro_login]','Member Sign In','','publish','closed','closed','','login','','','2026-07-17 16:14:43','2026-07-17 16:14:43','',0,'https://codesblock.com/login/',0,'page','',0),(25,1,'2026-07-17 16:14:43','2026-07-17 16:14:43','[pmpro_member_profile_edit]','Edit Profile','','publish','closed','closed','','edit-profile','','','2026-07-17 16:14:43','2026-07-17 16:14:43','',17,'https://codesblock.com/member-dashboard/edit-profile/',0,'page','',0),(26,1,'2026-07-17 16:14:43','2026-07-17 16:14:43','[codesblock_social_login]\n[pmpro_checkout]','Secure Checkout','','inherit','closed','closed','','20-revision-v1','','','2026-07-17 16:14:43','2026-07-17 16:14:43','',20,'https://codesblock.com/?p=26',0,'revision','',0),(27,0,'2026-08-21 13:52:52','2026-08-21 13:52:52','[nextend_social_login_register_flow]','Complete Your Profile','','publish','closed','closed','','complete-your-profile','','','2026-08-21 13:52:52','2026-08-21 13:52:52','',0,'https://codesblock.com/complete-your-profile/',0,'page','',0),(28,1,'2026-07-17 16:14:43','2026-07-17 16:14:43','<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Build agents that do useful work, not impressive demos</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This practical course takes you from a single tool-calling loop to a production-ready agent system with typed tools, durable state, evaluations, observability, and human approval gates. You will build a research-and-operations agent that can plan work, use APIs safely, recover from failures, and explain what it did.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The project</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You will ship an agent that receives a business question, gathers evidence from approved sources, produces a cited brief, and asks for approval before taking any external action. Every module adds one production concern to the same codebase.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How the course works</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><li>Short concept lessons followed by implementation labs</li><li>Architecture reviews that explain the tradeoffs</li><li>Failure-injection exercises for timeouts, malformed tool output, and prompt attacks</li><li>A final launch checklist covering cost, latency, privacy, and rollback</li></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Prerequisites</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You should be comfortable reading Python or TypeScript, calling a REST API, and using Git. Prior machine-learning experience is not required.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Build Production-Ready AI Agents','Design, build, evaluate, and ship reliable AI agents with safe tool use, memory, observability, and human approval.','publish','closed','closed','','build-production-ready-ai-agents','','','2026-07-17 16:14:43','2026-07-17 16:14:43','',0,'https://codesblock.com/courses/build-production-ready-ai-agents/',0,'course','',0),(29,0,'2026-07-17 16:59:25','2026-07-17 16:59:25','[nextend_social_login_register_flow]','Complete Your Profile','','inherit','closed','closed','','27-revision-v1','','','2026-07-17 16:59:25','2026-07-17 16:59:25','',27,'http://codesblock.com/?p=29',0,'revision','',0),(30,0,'2026-07-17 16:59:25','2026-07-17 16:59:25','<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Agent demos usually fail in production for ordinary software reasons: unclear permissions, weak error handling, missing measurements, and no safe way to stop. The model is only one component of the system.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. Give every tool a narrow contract</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Define accepted inputs, returned outputs, timeouts, and failure states. Reject unexpected fields before a tool reaches a database, browser, or external API.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. Separate suggestions from actions</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>An agent may draft an email, refund, deployment, or database change. A person or policy engine should approve consequential actions before they leave the system.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. Test the failures you expect</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list --><ul><li>Malformed or adversarial tool output</li><li>Rate limits, timeouts, and partial responses</li><li>Prompt injection inside retrieved content</li><li>Loops that consume the entire token or cost budget</li></ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4. Measure outcomes, not confidence</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Track task success, groundedness, latency, cost, human corrections, and unsafe action attempts. A confident answer is not evidence that the task was completed correctly.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The production checklist</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Ship with least-privilege tools, explicit stop conditions, durable traces, representative evaluations, privacy rules, human approval, budget limits, and a rollback plan. If one is missing, the agent is still a prototype.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Why AI Agents Fail in Production: 7 Guardrails That Matter','A practical review of the controls that turn an impressive agent demo into a system a team can operate safely.','inherit','closed','closed','','1-revision-v1','','','2026-07-17 16:59:25','2026-07-17 16:59:25','',1,'http://codesblock.com/?p=30',0,'revision','',0),(31,0,'2026-07-17 16:59:25','2026-07-17 16:59:25','<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>A strong system design answer is a sequence of decisions, not a tour of every technology you know. Use the clock to make your reasoning visible.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Minutes 0-5: clarify the problem</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Confirm users, core actions, consistency needs, latency expectations, geography, and what is explicitly out of scope. Write down the three requirements that will drive the architecture.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Minutes 5-10: estimate the load</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Use rounded assumptions for requests per second, storage growth, object size, and read-to-write ratio. The goal is to expose scale-sensitive choices, not to perform perfect arithmetic.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Minutes 10-25: draw the first complete path</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Show clients, APIs, data stores, queues, caches, and the main read and write flows. Start simple. Name the failure boundary and the source of truth.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Minutes 25-38: go deep where it matters</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list --><ul><li>Partitioning and hot-key risk</li><li>Consistency and duplicate processing</li><li>Cache invalidation and stale reads</li><li>Backpressure, retries, and dead-letter handling</li></ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Minutes 38-45: close with tradeoffs</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Summarize the design, the biggest risk, what you would measure, and the next improvement you would make with more time. Interviewers remember a clear close.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->','System Design Interview: A 45-Minute Answer Framework','A calm, repeatable structure for requirements, scale, architecture, bottlenecks, and tradeoffs under interview pressure.','publish','closed','open','','system-design-interview-45-minute-framework','','','2026-07-17 16:59:25','2026-07-17 16:59:25','',0,'http://codesblock.com/system-design-interview-45-minute-framework/',0,'post','',0),(32,0,'2026-07-17 16:59:25','2026-07-17 16:59:25','<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Before changing prompts or models, write down what a good result means. A small, representative evaluation set is more useful than dozens of polished screenshots.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Build cases from real work</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Collect normal requests, difficult edge cases, ambiguous inputs, and hostile content. Remove sensitive data and preserve the structure of the task.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Score the dimensions separately</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list --><ul><li>Task completion and factual support</li><li>Safety and policy compliance</li><li>Latency and cost</li><li>Clarity for the person who must use the result</li></ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Keep human review in the loop</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Automated graders help with scale, but a recurring human review catches subtle regressions. Record disagreements and turn them into better rubrics or new test cases.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ship with a rollback threshold</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Decide in advance which failure rate, latency increase, or cost spike pauses the rollout. Evaluations are most valuable when they drive an operational decision.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->','From Prompt to Production: Evaluate AI Features Before Launch','A lightweight evaluation loop for teams shipping LLM features without relying on vibes or cherry-picked demos.','publish','closed','open','','evaluate-ai-features-before-launch','','','2026-07-17 16:59:25','2026-07-17 16:59:25','',0,'http://codesblock.com/evaluate-ai-features-before-launch/',0,'post','',0),(33,0,'2026-07-17 16:59:25','2026-07-17 16:59:25','<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Senior interviews reward judgment. The strongest stories show the constraints you saw, the decision you owned, the tradeoff you accepted, and what changed because of your work.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Start with the engineering tension</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Replace “I built a service” with the real tension: reliability versus speed, migration risk versus product deadlines, or team autonomy versus platform consistency.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Make your decision visible</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Explain the options, the evidence you gathered, who you involved, and why the chosen path was appropriate at that moment. Avoid pretending there was only one correct answer.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Show leverage beyond your own code</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list --><ul><li>A decision framework another team reused</li><li>An incident practice that reduced recovery time</li><li>A migration plan that made delivery safer</li><li>Mentoring that changed ownership or quality</li></ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Close with the honest lesson</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Name what you would change now. A credible reflection demonstrates stronger judgment than a story where every decision appears perfect.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Senior Engineer Interviews: Turn Project Work Into Strong Evidence','A practical way to turn architecture, delivery, and incident work into concise senior-level interview stories.','publish','closed','open','','senior-engineer-interview-stories','','','2026-07-17 16:59:25','2026-07-17 16:59:25','',0,'http://codesblock.com/senior-engineer-interview-stories/',0,'post','',0),(34,1,'2026-07-17 16:59:25','2026-07-17 16:59:25','<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Build a system design answer you can explain, draw, and defend.</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>System Design Interview Lab turns vague prompts into a calm, repeatable method. You will clarify the problem, estimate the scale, draw a complete first architecture, choose components from constraints, and defend the trade-offs that matter. The goal is not to memorize finished diagrams. It is to build the judgment to design a system in front of another engineer.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Learn deeply, without getting stuck</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Read the lesson, form your own answer, then use the study companion when a sentence or decision needs a clearer explanation. Highlight a concept to unpack it, ask for a trade-off, test yourself with an interviewer-style follow-up, or return to your notes and architecture sketch.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What you will leave with</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><li>A reusable interview framework for open-ended design prompts</li><li>An estimation and architecture playbook you can adapt to new systems</li><li>Hands-on practice with core building blocks and full product designs</li><li>Clear notes on scalability, reliability, consistency, cost, and operational trade-offs</li><li>Mock-interview preparation and a capstone architecture review</li></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','System Design Interview Lab: Learn, Draw &amp; Defend','Build the confidence to design scalable systems, explain your choices clearly, and handle interview follow-ups. Learn by reading, sketching, testing, and defending real architecture decisions with an AI study companion.','publish','closed','closed','','system-design-interview-lab','','','2026-08-12 14:14:11','2026-08-12 14:14:11','',0,'http://codesblock.com/courses/system-design-interview-sprint/',0,'course','',0),(35,0,'2026-07-17 16:59:25','2026-07-17 16:59:25','<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Stop memorizing isolated solutions</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This free starter course teaches how to recognize and apply sliding windows, two pointers, hash maps, stacks, trees, graphs, and dynamic programming.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Practice format</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Each lesson includes a recognition clue, a worked example, complexity notes, and a short problem set.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->','DSA Patterns With Python','Learn the small set of reusable patterns behind common coding interview problems.','publish','closed','closed','','dsa-patterns-with-python','','','2026-07-17 16:59:25','2026-07-17 16:59:25','',0,'http://codesblock.com/courses/dsa-patterns-with-python/',0,'course','',0),(36,1,'2026-07-17 16:59:26','2026-07-17 16:59:26','<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Build an LLM feature your team can trust</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Move beyond prompt tweaking. You will create a retrieval-backed assistant, measure its behavior, inspect traces, and ship it behind a controlled rollout.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The project</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>A support copilot that cites approved knowledge, abstains when evidence is weak, and reports quality, latency, and cost.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Reliable LLM Apps: Evals, RAG, and Observability','Build an evidence-backed LLM feature with retrieval, evaluations, tracing, cost controls, and a safe rollout.','publish','closed','closed','','reliable-llm-apps','','','2026-08-16 08:18:40','2026-08-16 08:18:40','',0,'http://codesblock.com/courses/reliable-llm-apps/',0,'course','',0),(38,1,'2026-07-17 19:44:38','2026-07-17 19:44:38','','Test #38','','publish','closed','closed','','38-2','','','2026-07-17 19:45:08','2026-07-17 19:45:08','',0,'https://codesblock.com/?post_type=pronamic_gateway&#038;p=38',0,'pronamic_gateway','',0),(39,1,'2026-07-17 19:44:38','2026-07-17 19:44:38','','Test #38','','inherit','closed','closed','','38-revision-v1','','','2026-07-17 19:44:38','2026-07-17 19:44:38','',38,'https://codesblock.com/?p=39',0,'revision','',0),(40,1,'2026-07-17 19:56:49','2026-07-17 19:56:49','{\"id\":40,\"order_id\":\"1784318209\",\"key\":\"pay_6a5a8901de017\",\"description\":\"Test 1784318209\",\"customer\":{\"name\":{\"initials\":\"C.\",\"first_name\":\"codes\",\"last_name\":\"block\"},\"email\":\"dev-email@wpengine.local\",\"ip_address\":\"::1\",\"user_agent\":\"Mozilla\\/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit\\/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome\\/150.0.0.0 Safari\\/537.36 Edg\\/150.0.0.0\",\"language\":\"en\",\"locale\":\"en_US\",\"user_id\":1},\"billing_address\":{\"name\":{\"initials\":\"C.\",\"first_name\":\"codes\",\"last_name\":\"block\"},\"email\":\"dev-email@wpengine.local\",\"line_1\":\"Billing Line 1\",\"street_name\":\"Billing Line\",\"house_number\":{\"value\":\"1\",\"base\":\"1\"},\"postal_code\":\"1234 AB\",\"city\":\"Billing City\",\"country\":{\"code\":\"NL\"}},\"shipping_address\":{\"name\":{\"initials\":\"C.\",\"first_name\":\"codes\",\"last_name\":\"block\"},\"email\":\"dev-email@wpengine.local\",\"line_1\":\"Shipping Line 1\",\"street_name\":\"Shipping Line\",\"house_number\":{\"value\":\"1\",\"base\":\"1\"},\"postal_code\":\